On 12 avr, 03:45, Brad Larson <bklar...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I just beat Medusa with my lvl17 Val.  My only other time to
> make it this far was when I happened to find a WoW in the very
> early game.

> I currently have a +3 burnt small shield, should I stick with
> this or switch to the shield of reflection I picked up off
> Perseus?  I have a single magic marker, so I could probably
> enhance it a bit.  My AC is currently -11

That's less than I like to have at that level.  Between buying
protection and testing BUC-id'ed armor to find something
enchanted, you should really be able to do better.  (I'm not
sure it's that important, though.  Getting distinctly negative
is, but once you're well into the negative range, I don't notice
a really big difference until the planes.  By which time, you'll
have your quest artifact, which in the case of Valk, effectively
doubles your hit points.)

> Also, which weapon should I be using?  I have Excalibur at +1
> and Mjollnir at 0, as well as a small collection of Elven
> daggers.  I'm expert at all 3... which should I use my scrolls
> of EW on?  Or should I hold off for a better weapon?

Excalibur's one of the best there is.  I tend to prefer it to
Grayswandir, even, until I've got magic resistence---it's
automatic searching makes avoiding poly-traps considerably
easier.

At this point, I'd rather try to see if I couldn't stay less
than, say, AC -5 without a shield, and start two-weaponing.
Below the castle, unless you've got Grayswandir, you'll probably
want a silver sabre in your off hand, and above, that second hit
with a long sword or such can also do a lot of damage.  (FWIW, I
certainly wouldn't have bothered with advancing Mjollnir, and
would probably have left Excalibur at skilled until I had two
weapon up there as well.)

